  "description": "Cue words for the deterministic direction check in scripts/verify_claims.py. Matched case-insensitively as whole words or phrases in the evidence span. A span's direction is the product of the signs of its directional cues (up = +1, down = -1) when it has one or two such cues and no contrast word; when the span supports a single claim, a printed ratio estimate (OR, HR, RR) gives +1 when every ratio is above 1 and -1 when every ratio is below 1. When the cue sign and the ratio sign disagree, or neither exists, the lexicon cannot decide and the claim is direction_unverified.",
